WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:06.902
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, I asked all
of you to submit your Walking Dead Questions

00:00:06.902 --> 00:00:09.700
after Episode 11 and I’ve picked 10 to answer
in a video with one fun bonus question.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.530
I’ve also got a new winner to announce in
my weekly Walking Dead Giveaway.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:15.700
If you’re finding me for the first time
Each week I pick a random subscriber from

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:19.289
the comments to give an amazon gift card to
just as a way to say thank you for being so

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:20.289
awesome.

00:00:20.289 --> 00:00:23.600
Round 4 will start when I post my Episode
12 review next Sunday night.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.179
Until then everyone be sure to give Lauriita
Mercury a high five because she is this week’s

00:00:27.179 --> 00:00:28.179
winner.

00:00:28.179 --> 00:00:30.180
I’ll be messaging you on your channel for
details.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.560
Now let’s answer some mullets.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.760
Questions, I mean questions.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.200
Number 1 - Cameron Peter asks Do you think
Rick and Carl will find out that Judith is

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.560
alive soon?﻿

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:44.510
I think they’ll run into Tyreese and Carol’s
group before the season finale, they’re

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.300
both headed towards Sanctuary.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.510
I think it will take a few more episodes at
least.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:52.930
The show is playing this weird trick where
in the comics Sanctuary comes after Alexandria,

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:57.010
so they might be combining those two places
or they might all get to Sanctuary and Leave

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:58.010
early.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:02.400
I don’t really think they’d combine two
places that had major storylines in the books,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.280
so it will probably be a week or two before
we get a better answer.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:10.229
Question 2 - Milena Torres asks Do you think
the next episode will be focus on Daryl?

00:01:10.229 --> 00:01:13.330
Perhaps showing his past as in the case of
Michonne?

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:19.289
Yes, based on the teaser they’re just going
to cover all the people that they skipped

00:01:19.289 --> 00:01:24.380
this week, which is Daryl and Beth and Tyreese’s
Group.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:27.720
We didn’t get a super deep look into any
of the characters in episode 10.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:31.429
So the mere fact Daryl and Beth took up the
whole teaser implies that they’ll have the

00:01:31.429 --> 00:01:33.999
biggest WTF moment of the episode.

00:01:33.999 --> 00:01:37.969
Say your prayers for Beth.

00:01:37.969 --> 00:01:42.049
Question 3 - Li Cheng (no avatar) asks Do
you think they ever will make a prequel movie

00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:44.079
about the walking dead?

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:46.100
There have been a lot of rumors that the spinoff
tv series that Robert Kirkman is in charge

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.450
of is going to be a prequel.

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:51.109
I don’t believe that, but it’s more likely
that they’d tell the prequel bits in comic

00:01:51.109 --> 00:01:52.109
book flashbacks.

00:01:52.109 --> 00:01:55.850
I don’t really consider the flashbacks that
people on the show like Michonne have to be

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:57.369
prequel storylines.

00:01:57.369 --> 00:01:59.100
At least in the way I think you’re implying.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:02.139
They’re not really going to tell the story
of how the outbreak started.

00:02:02.139 --> 00:02:07.579
We’ll definitely learn more about individual
characters before the outbreak though.

00:02:07.579 --> 00:02:11.600
Question 4 - George Barrett asks Do you really
think they'd reveal a cure?

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.130
No, I don’t think Robert Kirkman will do
that in the comics and I don’t think that

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:17.280
Scott Gimple would do that on the show.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.060
If they did it would automatically create
an endpoint for the series.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.610
Logically curing the outbreak, which would
force the show to end at a certain point.

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:28.590
They will end the main show eventually just
because everyone will get burned out and people’s

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.630
salaries will get to expensive.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:34.670
But Robert Kirkman said he’ll continue making
the comic as long as people keep buying it,

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:35.680
which is basically forever.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.860
And as long as he keeps writing new stories,
the show will have new material to draw from.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.130
The spinoff will be the big test though.

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:45.850
It’s going to be completely new characters
that weren’t in the comics.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:49.660
If that does well, then you can bet that walking
dead will remain on television in some form

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:55.950
for at least the next 5 years.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:03:01.550
Question 5 - Chrocks09 (no avatar) asks Do
you think negan will be introduced this season?

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:04.120
No, or at least if he is.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.140
It won’t be till the final moments.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:09.570
In the comics he doesn’t debut till way
way later than where they are right now.

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:13.230
So the show would have to skip a lot of stuff
to bring him out.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:15.490
The Hunters on the other hand are much closer.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:20.290
They haven’t confirmed them, but I did include
a few more Hunter related questions in this

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:21.290
Q&amp;A.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:26.700
Question 6 - Ehsan0121 asks Will the whole
group meet up at the end of the season?

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:32.430
The whole group no, but I’m considering
Dary and Beth to be one group, Tyreese and

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:38.040
Carol another, Rick and Michonne are one,
Maggie, Sasha and Bob are one and Abraham

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.820
and Glenn make 5 separate groups right now.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:45.120
By the end of the season I think that at least
two of those groups will merge with others.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.780
I think everyone headed toward Sanctuary will
meet up.

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:50.090
Meaning Rick and Carl will be reunited with
Baby Judith.

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:54.100
And I think that Glenn will find Maggie, meaning
Abraham’s group will merge with hers.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.730
That kind of leaves Daryl and Beth on their
own.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:04:01.030
I think it will be a couple more episodes
before we see groups getting closer so it’ll

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:04.400
be easier to make an educated guess on how
it’s going to go down then.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:09.370
Question 7 - lalov1 asks Do you think the
show will make Abraham seem good to only turn

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.840
out to be bad later?

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.440
I think Abraham is trying to do good.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.370
I don’t think he’s like the Governor.

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:18.079
He does give off a really aggro vibe, but
it’s really Doctor Mullet we should be worried

00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:19.079
about.

00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:24.600
He seems too stupid to know anything about
a cure, so keep your eyes on him for any creepy

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.720
episode ending smiles.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:31.050
Question 8 - Jane S (no avatar) asks I noticed
that the bad guy on the porch was Jeff Kober

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:33.340
(who always plays a bad guy).

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:37.189
Do you think that he and any other survivors
of the house will show up later?﻿

00:04:37.189 --> 00:04:43.749
Yes, Negan’s group the Saviors have a kind
of biker look to them and he kind of looked

00:04:43.749 --> 00:04:45.969
like he was dressed like that.

00:04:45.969 --> 00:04:49.349
My first thought was Hunters, but the show
hasn’t confirmed that group will make an

00:04:49.349 --> 00:04:50.349
appearance.

00:04:50.349 --> 00:04:52.130
So for now I’ll just say yes.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:54.999
They’ll be back, I just can’t confirm
who exactly they are.

00:04:54.999 --> 00:04:58.421
Question 9 - The Turtle Gamer asks do you
think rick or Carl could die this season,

00:04:58.421 --> 00:05:00.050
do you think the people in the house could
be a part of a bigger group?﻿

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:03.000
No, but someone from the prison is supposed
to die.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:08.990
The big rumor is that it’s someone from
the comics who’s still alive in the comics.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:11.610
I know that sounds weird, but that’s what
the rumor said.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:15.169
Which really narrows it down, meaning Beth
and Daryl would be safe.

00:05:15.169 --> 00:05:18.199
But it puts Maggie on the chopping block potentially.

00:05:18.199 --> 00:05:21.699
So cross your fingers and be prepared for
a big WTF.

00:05:21.699 --> 00:05:24.080
I think whoever it ends up being, we’ll
be surprised.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:28.990
I didn’t know what was going to happen to
Herschel in episode 8.

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:34.349
Question 10 - Cristian Hernandez (no avatar)
asks Would go find Maggie or Save the world?

00:05:34.349 --> 00:05:39.030
This is the classic Star Trek conundrum, the
needs of the one versus the needs of the many.

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:40.169
Of course I would go save Maggie.

00:05:40.169 --> 00:05:42.289
I’m a human being and deeply flawed.

00:05:42.289 --> 00:05:45.580
Glenn kind of represents the everyman, like
a totally normal person.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:48.720
And he’s not going to care about anything
BUT Maggie.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.439
For him it’s not a choice at all.

00:05:50.439 --> 00:05:53.650
He was going to smash the shit out of that
window to get them to stop.

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:57.969
It only seems like he’s making a poor choice,
but really I thought he was the only one actually

00:05:57.969 --> 00:05:58.969
using his brain.

00:05:58.969 --> 00:06:01.309
Even though it seemed like he was only using
his heart.

00:06:01.309 --> 00:06:06.939
Bonus Question - teebaby0486 asks The people
in Rick’s House, I got a hunter vibe from

00:06:06.939 --> 00:06:09.979
them, but if they're not the hunters who are
they?

00:06:09.979 --> 00:06:12.699
The other major group they could be is The
Saviors.

00:06:12.699 --> 00:06:15.590
If you want to learn more about them you can
check out the comic books.

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:18.819
But the saviors are associated with Sanctuary
and Negan.

00:06:18.819 --> 00:06:21.310
Which is like this big looming threat in the
distance.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:25.101
I really hope the show doesn’t go there
this fast, it will probably be a couple of

00:06:25.101 --> 00:06:27.939
weeks before we get a better picture of how
that’s all going to go down.

00:06:27.939 --> 00:06:32.110
There’s at least one more major new character
named Gareth that hasn’t appeared yet.

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:36.620
I’m expecting to see him next week or in
episode 13.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:40.860
Supposedly he’s going to be a new antagonist
that’s an amalgam of a couple of different

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:41.860
comic book characters.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.360
So thanks so much for submitting your questions.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:45.059
This was a lot of fun as always.

00:06:45.059 --> 00:06:49.449
I tried to combine a few answers since a lot
of you had similar questions.

